Subject: Make the gradient and texture float-to-int conversions defined

plutovg-blend.c casts floats to int in its gradient lookups and texture
fetchers. A gradient over a degenerate geometry yields a NaN position, and
a degenerate texture transform a value out of int's range; either cast is
undefined behaviour (UBSan: "-nan is outside the range of representable
values of type 'int'", found by zusvg's fuzzer at plutovg-blend.c:195).
The texture fetchers then step their 16.16 positions across the span in
int, which an out-of-range step overflows.

plutovg_f2i() maps NaN to 0 and clamps to +-2^30; plutovg_f2l() does the
same in 64 bits to +-2^46, and the texture positions and steps become
int64_t, so stepping across a span cannot overflow. Ordinary gradients and
textures convert exactly as before.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §9. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutovg/source/plutovg-blend.c
+++ b/plutovg/source/plutovg-blend.c
@@ -161,6 +161,31 @@
 
 #endif // __SSE2__
 
+/* float to integer conversions that are defined for every input: a NaN is
+ * 0, and values are clamped, so a degenerate transform or gradient cannot
+ * make a cast (or a later addition) undefined. */
+static inline int plutovg_f2i(float v)
+{
+    if(v != v)
+        return 0;
+    if(v <= -1073741824.f)
+        return -1073741824;
+    if(v >= 1073741824.f)
+        return 1073741824;
+    return (int)v;
+}
+
+static inline int64_t plutovg_f2l(float v)
+{
+    if(v != v)
+        return 0;
+    if(v <= -70368744177664.f)
+        return -70368744177664LL;
+    if(v >= 70368744177664.f)
+        return 70368744177664LL;
+    return (int64_t)v;
+}
+
 static inline int gradient_clamp(const gradient_data_t* gradient, int ipos)
 {
     if(gradient->spread == PLUTOVG_SPREAD_METHOD_REPEAT) {
@@ -192,7 +217,7 @@
 
